From 4047ac4f0746cd2836b3f47505f2f3ade52d23b7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: niyue <n1yu3@proton.me>
Date: Mon, 10 Aug 2026 13:20:20 +0800
Subject: codEx fork: Linux-only release, /rewind, double-Esc interrupt,
 pure-Rust update, patch-queue model

- Trim release/CI to Linux + CLI only; add fork release archives (codex-<target>.tar.gz + sha256)
- Add /rewind: conversation rollback via searchable picker and plain-file workspace snapshots
- Esc is a no-op on single press; double Esc within 400ms stops a running reply
- Disable update check on startup by default; remove announcement fetch
- codex update now downloads and sha256-verifies fork binaries in pure Rust
- Brand CLI/status bar as codEx; version stays aligned with the base tag
- Add patch-queue tooling (BASE_TAG, bootstrap/update/gen-patches) and fork README
